Z||000003||coyote||03-23-2000||12:09 PM||||You can talk to Paul Vargas he is a member of N.I.F.E., he is very local to chicago or you can come on up and see what we have in the shop right now and talk to archie.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-23-2000||01:40 PM||||I was at the N.I.F.E. club meeting at Archies on the 18th of this month. He does real good work there. I even had a ride in an 88 Formula with a V-8! If you go to Archies website he has a description of what is involved. If your close enough I would suggest going and talking to Archie. He had 4 cars they were doing conversions on in his shop and you can see exactly how it's done. If I had the money I'd get a V-8!<P>As for N.I.F.E. it is the Northern Illinois Fiero Enthusiasts. Great club! Only $20 per year and you have access to a wealth of Fiero knowledge! You can check out their website if your interested in joining. Paul Vargyas is the membership director, His E-mail is at the NIFE website. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-23-2000||01:50 PM||||IMHO, I would only consider the Northstar 4.0/4,6L swap and even that is marginal.<P>I know there are V8's out there but from what I've seen, I don't consider them to be a practical installation. They plain don't fit. Anything that requires the belts to be on the outside of the car is not clean.<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||03-23-2000||09:26 PM||||Terry is right of course, but I still love my dirty V8 Fiero. My Mom warned me about dirty girls too, but I still "dated" a couple in my younger days and still had lots of fun with them too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||03-24-2000||12:06 AM||||I was at v8archies also.  Oreif, I couldn't ID you.  You didn't face paint on the fiero logo.<P>I still think I am going to do an LT1 conversion with an engine I got out of a Buick Roadmaster.  From what I saw with the LT1, I will have to do a frame notch and weld reinforcement.  However, that will leave the water pump belt inside and not out into the wheel well.  It may be a dirty solution, but sure would be a fun one.<P>The northstar conversion would be great, but with horsepower it's all about money.<P>You are close by.  Go to v8archie's shop.  It will be worth the trip.<P>Final point.  Being where you are from, shouldn't you be doing a v8 conversion on a pacer????  Wayne's world, Wayne's world!||||reg||7
Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||12:16 AM||||What about zumalt???? Is he still doing swaps?  last I heardn him and pizza were in together.  he centers the engine, and gives you stronger axles.  But I think a 3.8 supercharged, is alott more relaible and feisable and I did mine for about 3200 or so.  I know the v8 sounds tempting but, hey if you have ther time and the money do it!!!!!!!!!!!  Especially if you are that close to archies, I would be there everyday hanging out.  Hey maybe I could cruise up and down the street they are on and try and race them.  I would love to get left in tire smoke by a ls1 fiero more than I like getting left by a ls1 f-body. just my .02! ||||reg||1
